{"dirGan ca": [{"id": "dIrGaM ca", "headword": "दीर्घं च", "headword_slp1": "dIrGaM ca", "fold": "dirGan ca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "And a long vowel is also called गुरु 'heavy'.\n\nTerms: गुरु", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दीर्घं च १.४.१२", "१.४.१२", "१.४.१२ दीर्घं च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dIrGaM ca १.४.१२", "१.४.१२", "१.४.१२ dIrGaM ca"]}], "dirGajihvi ca cCandasi": [{"id": "dIrGajihvI ca cCandasi", "headword": "दीर्घजिह्वी च च्छन्दसि", "headword_slp1": "dIrGajihvI ca cCandasi", "fold": "dirGajihvi ca cCandasi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The form दीर्घजिह्वी 'long-tongued' is irregularly formed in the छन्दस् (Vedas).\n\nTerms: Irregular", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दीर्घजिह्वी च च्छन्दसि ४.१.५९", "४.१.५९", "४.१.५९ दीर्घजिह्वी च च्छन्दसि"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dIrGajihvI ca cCandasi ४.१.५९", "४.१.५९", "४.१.५९ dIrGajihvI ca cCandasi"]}], "dirGat‌": [{"id": "dIrGAt‌", "headword": "दीर्घात्‌", "headword_slp1": "dIrGAt‌", "fold": "dirGat‌", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The augment त् is added to a long vowel, when followed by छ in a continous text.\n\nTerms: संहितायाम्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दीर्घात्‌ ६.१.७५", "६.१.७५", "६.१.७५ दीर्घात्‌"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dIrGAt‌ ६.१.७५", "६.१.७५", "६.१.७५ dIrGAt‌"]}], "dirGajasi ca": [{"id": "dIrGAjjasi ca", "headword": "दीर्घाज्जसि च", "headword_slp1": "dIrGAjjasi ca", "fold": "dirGajasi ca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The substitution of a long vowel homogenous with the first, does not take place whena long vowel is followed by a nominative or accusative case-affix beginning with a vowel (other than अ) or by the Nominative Plural affix अस्।\n\nTerms: संहितायाम्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दीर्घाज्जसि च ६.१.१०५", "६.१.१०५", "६.१.१०५ दीर्घाज्जसि च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dIrGAjjasi ca ६.१.१०५", "६.१.१०५", "६.१.१०५ dIrGAjjasi ca"]}], "dirGakasatusaBraswravawan je": [{"id": "dIrGakASatuzaBrAzwravawaM je", "headword": "दीर्घकाशतुषभ्राष्ट्रवटं जे", "headword_slp1": "dIrGakASatuzaBrAzwravawaM je", "fold": "dirGakasatusaBraswravawan je", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "When the first member is a word ending in a long vowel or is 1. काश 2. तुष 3. भ्राष्ट्र 4. वट and is followed by ज , the acutely accented (उदात्त) falls on the first syllable.\n\nTerms: समास 1st-acute", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दीर्घकाशतुषभ्राष्ट्रवटं जे ६.२.८२", "६.२.८२", "६.२.८२ दीर्घकाशतुषभ्राष्ट्रवटं जे"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dIrGakASatuzaBrAzwravawaM je ६.२.८२", "६.२.८२", "६.२.८२ dIrGakASatuzaBrAzwravawaM je"]}], "dirGaca varuRasya": [{"id": "dIrGAcca varuRasya", "headword": "दीर्घाच्च वरुणस्य", "headword_slp1": "dIrGAcca varuRasya", "fold": "dirGaca varuRasya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "Before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् in a द्वन्द समास of god-names, the वृद्धि is not substituted for the first vowel of वरुण when a long vowel precedes it.\n\nTerms: वृद्धि", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दीर्घाच्च वरुणस्य ७.३.२३", "७.३.२३", "७.३.२३ दीर्घाच्च वरुणस्य"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dIrGAcca varuRasya ७.३.२३", "७.३.२३", "७.३.२३ dIrGAcca varuRasya"]}], "dirGa iRaH kiti": [{"id": "dIrGa iRaH kiti", "headword": "दीर्घ इणः किति", "headword_slp1": "dIrGa iRaH kiti", "fold": "dirGa iRaH kiti", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "A long vowel is substituted in the reduplicate of the root इ (एति) before a personal ending of the लिट् (Perfect Tense), which has an indicatory क्।\n\nTerms: Reduplicate", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दीर्घ इणः किति ७.४.६९", "७.४.६९", "७.४.६९ दीर्घ इणः किति"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dIrGa iRaH kiti ७.४.६९", "७.४.६९", "७.४.६९ dIrGa iRaH kiti"]}], "dirGokitaH": [{"id": "dIrGo'kitaH", "headword": "दीर्घोऽकितः", "headword_slp1": "dIrGo'kitaH", "fold": "dirGokitaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "A long vowel is substituted for the अ of the reduplicate in the Intensive (with expressed or elided यङ्) when the reduplicate receives no augment having an indicatory क् ।\n\nTerms: Reduplicate", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दीर्घोऽकितः ७.४.८३", "७.४.८३", "७.४.८३ दीर्घोऽकितः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dIrGo'kitaH ७.४.८३", "७.४.८३", "७.४.८३ dIrGo'kitaH"]}], "dirGo laGoH": [{"id": "dIrGo laGoH", "headword": "दीर्घो लघोः", "headword_slp1": "dIrGo laGoH", "fold": "dirGo laGoH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In the reduplicative syllable, a prosodially short vowel is lengthened in the reduplicated Aorist of the Causative when the vowel of the root is light and the root has not lost its end-vowel before the Causative णि।\n\nTerms: Reduplicate", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दीर्घो लघोः ७.४.९४", "७.४.९४", "७.४.९४ दीर्घो लघोः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dIrGo laGoH ७.४.९४", "७.४.९४", "७.४.९४ dIrGo laGoH"]}], "dirGadawi samanapade": [{"id": "dIrGAdawi samAnapade", "headword": "दीर्घादटि समानपदे", "headword_slp1": "dIrGAdawi samAnapade", "fold": "dirGadawi samanapade", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "रु is optionally substituted for that final न् of a word which is preceded by a long vowel and is followed by a letter of the अट् प्रत्यहार (vowel or semi-vowel with the exception of ल्) when these (न् and अट्) come in contact with each other in the same stanza of the ऋग्वेद।\n\nTerms: Nasal रु", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दीर्घादटि समानपदे ८.३.९", "८.३.९", "८.३.९ दीर्घादटि समानपदे"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dIrGAdawi samAnapade ८.३.९", "८.३.९", "८.३.९ dIrGAdawi samAnapade"]}], "dirGadacaryaRam": [{"id": "dIrGAdAcAryARAm", "headword": "दीर्घादाचार्याणाम्", "headword_s